{title: For the Beauty of the Earth}
{artist: Folliott S. Pierpoint / Conrad Kocher}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: for-the-beauty-of-the-earth.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]For the beauty of the [C]earth
[G]For the glory of the [D]skies
[G]For the love which from our [C]birth
O[G]ver and a[D]round us [G]lies
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Lord of all, to [C]Thee we raise
[G]This our hymn of [D]grate[G]ful praise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]For the beauty of each [C]hour
[G]Of the day and of the [D]night
[G]Hill and vale, and tree and [C]flower
[G]Sun and moon, and [D]stars of [G]light
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]For the joy of ear and [C]eye
[G]For the heart and mind's de[D]light
[G]For the mystic har[C]mony
[G]Linking sense to [D]sound and [G]sight
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]For the joy of human [C]love
[G]Brother, sister, parent, [D]child
[G]Friends on earth, and friends a[C]bove
[G]For all gentle [D]thoughts and [G]mild
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]For Thy Church that ever[C]more
[G]Lifteth holy hands a[D]bove
[G]Offering up on every [C]shore
[G]Her pure sacri[D]fice of [G]love
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
